<?xml version='1.0' encoding='utf-8'?>
<graphml xmlns="http://graphml.graphdrawing.org/xmlns" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:schemaLocation="http://graphml.graphdrawing.org/xmlns http://graphml.graphdrawing.org/xmlns/1.0/graphml.xsd">
  <key id="d6" for="edge" attr.name="source_id" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d5" for="edge" attr.name="keywords" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d4" for="edge" attr.name="description" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d3" for="edge" attr.name="weight" attr.type="double" />
  <key id="d2" for="node" attr.name="source_id" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d1" for="node" attr.name="description" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d0" for="node" attr.name="entity_type" attr.type="string" />
  <graph edgedefault="undirected">
    <node id="&quot;PHILIP LOWRIE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Philip Lowrie is a British actor who arrived in Japan in 1965 to immerse himself in the language and culture, with a particular interest in Japan stemming from his early fascination with 'The Tale of Genji'."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0047</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FUKUOKA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Fukuoka is a city in Japan where Philip Lowrie arrived and began his immersion in Japanese culture."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0047</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;KYUSHU UNIVERSITY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Kyushu University is the institution where Philip Lowrie stayed during his time in Japan, studying the Japanese language and culture."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0047</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;1965&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"1965 marks the year when Philip Lowrie arrived in Japan to begin his cultural immersion."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0047</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BBC'S 'CORONATION STREET'&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"BBC's 'Coronation Street' is a television show that Philip Lowrie was known for before arriving in Japan."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0047</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;USED BOOKSTORE IN MANCHESTER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A used bookstore in Manchester is where Philip Lowrie first encountered 'The Tale of Genji', sparking his interest in Japan."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0047</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;THE TALE OF GENJI&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Tale of Genji is a literary work that captivated Philip Lowrie and influenced his interest in Japan."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0047</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MAPLE TREES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Maple trees are part of the natural scenery in Fukuoka that Philip Lowrie noticed during his arrival."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0047</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;KOYO&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Koyo, or the changing leaves of the maple trees, is a seasonal phenomenon that Philip Lowrie experienced in Fukuoka."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0047</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PROFESSOR TANAKA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Professor Tanaka is a linguist at Kyushu University who welcomed Philip Lowrie and helped him with his studies."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0047</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GREEN TEA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Green tea is a beverage that Philip Lowrie enjoyed during his stay at Kyushu University."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0047</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;KANJI&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Kanji is a component of the Japanese writing system that Philip Lowrie studied intensively during his time at Kyushu University."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0047</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STUDENTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Students at Kyushu University are Philip Lowrie's peers and fellow learners in his language and culture studies."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0047</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RAMEN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Ramen is a traditional Japanese dish that Philip Lowrie enjoyed at the campus cafeteria during his stay."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0047</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;THEATER TROUPE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The theater troupe at Kyushu University is a group of students performing a production of 'Hamlet' in Japanese, which Philip Lowrie joined."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0047</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SET DESIGN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Set design is a part of the theater troupe's activities that Philip Lowrie contributed to during his stay at Kyushu University."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0047</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ROYAL ACADEMY OF DRAMATIC ART (RADA)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"RADA is a prestigious drama school in London where Philip Lowrie attended and graduated from."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0047</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LONDON, ENGLAND&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"London, England is the location of RADA, where Philip Lowrie received his education in acting."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0047</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;POPULAR TV SERIES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Popular TV series are a category of television shows where Philip Lowrie has appeared after his graduation from RADA."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0047</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MANCHESTER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Manchester is the city where Philip Lowrie first encountered 'The Tale of Genji' in a used bookstore."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0047</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;JAPAN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Japan is the country where Philip Lowrie traveled to immerse himself in the language and culture."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0047</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;THEATER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The theater at Kyushu University is where Philip Lowrie participated in the 'Hamlet' production."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0047</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SHAKESPEARE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Shakespeare is the playwright whose works, including 'Hamlet', Philip Lowrie studied and performed in Japanese."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0047</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LEFT AND RIGHT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Left and right are terms that Philip Lowrie struggled with while learning the Japanese language."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0047</data>
    </node>
    <edge source="&quot;PHILIP LOWRIE&quot;" target="&quot;FUKUOKA&quot;">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Philip Lowrie arrived in Fukuoka, a city in Japan, to immerse himself in the language and culture."</data>
      <data key="d5">"immersion, arrival"</data>
      <data key="d6">cb-0047</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;PHILIP LOWRIE&quot;" target="&quot;KYUSHU UNIVERSITY&quot;">
      <data key="d3">9.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Philip Lowrie stayed at Kyushu University to study the Japanese language and culture."</data>
      <data key="d5">"study, residence"</data>
      <data key="d6">cb-0047</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;PHILIP LOWRIE&quot;" target="&quot;1965&quot;">
      <data key="d3">7.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"1965 marks the year when Philip Lowrie arrived in Japan to begin his cultural immersion."</data>
      <data key="d5">"time period, arrival"</data>
      <data key="d6">cb-0047</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;PHILIP LOWRIE&quot;" target="&quot;BBC'S 'CORONATION STREET'&quot;">
      <data key="d3">6.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Philip Lowrie was known for his role in the television show 'Coronation Street' before arriving in Japan."</data>
      <data key="d5">"fame, prior work"</data>
      <data key="d6">cb-0047</data>
    </edge>
  </graph>
